7592186426855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426857 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112247" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426857 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426857 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426857 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad22bfb4-da83-594b-af3c-ca1a05478310" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426857 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-3)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-4)+(-3)=-7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426858 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426858 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "23a4ea36-89a6-56d3-bf56-d577c8099f1a" #edb/ref 17592186